{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Before the gray head you shall stand.</b> But you shall honor those who are holy to the Most High — and among them, the gray-headed in the majority, as it says: עֲטֶרֶת תִּפְאֶרֶת שֵׂיבָה, בְּדֶרֶךְ צְדָקָה תִּמָּצֵא (Proverbs 16:31)." "<b>And you shall honor the face of the elder.</b> These are the masters of Torah, as our Sages of blessed memory said: אֵין זָקֵן אֶלָּא מִי שֶׁקָּנָה חָכְמָה (Kiddushin 32b). And after warning concerning the honor due to the holy, He warned against despising the lowly, and said:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:02.726573312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}